# =============================================================================
# COMP 482 project — Git ignore
#
# Python project (docs/plan.md, D8). Build tools generate large folders the
# moment they first run; one `git add -A` without these rules puts them in
# history.
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem

# --- Data and results --------------------------------------------------------
# Large datasets are downloaded by a script into data/raw/, never committed.
# results/ IS committed: the report's tables and plots are evidence.
data/raw/
results/tmp/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- IDE and editor files ----------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.vs/
*.swp
*~

# --- OS files ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Claude Code -------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/settings.json is committed. Personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway scripts, notes and outputs. Anything worth keeping moves into the
# repository proper (results go in docs/llm-wiki/findings.md).
/.scratch/
*.local
